  "evidence": "The pad syllable of padmo (lotus) has dropped out. Four checks, each run against the shipped spine. (1) The facing English of this very segment reads \"I bow to the lotus feet\"; as the wylie now stands there is no syllable anywhere in the segment that can license \"lotus\". (2) A token census of every standalone \"mor\" in the spine returns 136 occurrences, and C03:297 is the ONLY one preceded by a genitive particle: a LIKE scan for 'kyi mor' / 'gyi mor' / ' gi mor' / \"'i mor\" returns exactly one row, this segment. Every other mor sits on a lexical stem with its head intact (rtse mor 21x, phra mor 17x, lha mor 12x, mtshan mor 11x, chen mor 9x, nyin mor 9x, ri mor 7x; e.g. C01:239 'lam rim chen mor', C03:137 'sna'i rtse mor', C03:399 'mtshan mor', C06:167 'nyin mor', C01:478 'ri mor'). (3) The identical construction is attested intact, spelled as one token: TCS18Commentary:17 reads \"bla ma'i (zhabs kyi padmor te) zhabs nyid padmar bkod pa de la'o\" and TCS18Commentary:116 reads \"bla ma'i (zhabs) kyi (padmor) te zhabs de nyid la padmo'i ming gis bstan nas\" -- and the facing English of both of those segments renders it \"lotus feet\". Further parallels: TCS18LamaChupa:34 \"rdo rje can zhabs padmor phyag 'tshal lo\" (English: \"I bow down to the lotus feet\"), TCS18LamaChupa:4 \"rdo rje can zhabs padmor gus btud nas\"; the la-variant at TCS14:34 \"zhabs kyi padmo la gus pa chen pos phyag 'tshal lo\" and TCS10:87 \"zhabs kyi padmo la gus pas 'dud pa\"; and the pad+m- spellings at TCS05:26 \"bla ma'i zhabs kyi pad+mara ji bzhin btud\" and TCS03:415 \"rje rdo rje 'chang zhabs pad+mora 'dud\". (4) The expected form is given as the single token 'padmor' rather than a spaced 'pad mor' because that is what the spine uses in this exact construction (padmor, 9 occurrences); a spaced 'pad mo' occurs only twice in the whole spine (C09:167, TITLS:3070) and in neither is it this formula.",
