  "expected": "You Should Give Up.  [footnote 1]",
  "evidence": "CLASS ENTRY, not a single instance. Printed footnote reference numbers have been flattened into the running English at ingest, fused to the sentence-final period with no separator. Measured across the whole spine: 307 occurrences in 281 segments across 5 courses - C01 161, C03 95, C16 38, TCS13 7, TCS15 6. Counted on the signature 'sentence-final punctuation + 1-3 digits + space + capital', which excludes thousands separators ('25,000'), section labels ('(S1)') and verse citations ('[I.1b]'); two looser patterns were tried first and gave 1,054 and 867 before those contaminants were excluded. Every instance breaks exact-match search on the final word of its sentence.",
